### Core API — REST Client (End-to-End Flow)
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}
@tenantId = 1
@siteId = 1
@userId = 1
@roleId = 1
@permissionId = 1

### ============================================================
### STEP 1. LOGIN & GET FORMATTED MENU
### ============================================================

### 1.1 Login (Returns JWT token + user_info + formatted menu in data.meta)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "admin@primary.localhost",
    "password": "password123"
}


### ============================================================
### STEP 2. FETCH SCHEMA VIA MENU LINK (CREATE & EDIT MODES)
### ============================================================

### 2.1 Fetch Users Schema for Create (No id -> returns schema + default empty model)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/access/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.2 Fetch Users Schema for Edit (With id -> populates model with DB record)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/access/users&id={{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.3 Fetch Roles Schema via Menu Link
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/access/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.4 Fetch Tenants Schema via Menu Link (Create)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/tenancy/tenants
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.5 Fetch Tenants Schema via Menu Link (Edit Tenant #1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/tenancy/tenants&id={{tenantId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 2.6 Fetch Sites Schema via Menu Link (Edit Site #1)
GET {{baseUrl}}/schema?link=core/tenancy/sites&id={{siteId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### STEP 3. CREATE ROLES (MODULE-BASED & STANDARD)
### ============================================================

### 3.1 Create Role with Module-Based Permissions (All Core permissions except delete actions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role_name": "Branch Manager",
    "description": "Manages branch users, sites, and roles",
    "modules": ["Core"],
    "permissions": [],
    "except": [
        "core.tenancy.tenants.delete",
        "core.access.users.delete",
        "core.access.roles.delete"
    ]
}

### 3.2 Create Role with Specific Module Permissions Only
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role_name": "Support Officer",
    "description": "Can view users and reset passwords",
    "modules": ["Core"],
    "permissions": [
        "core.access.users.view",
        "core.access.users.activate.execute",
        "core.access.users.reset-password.execute"
    ],
    "except": []
}

### 3.3 Create Blank/Standard Role (Using Schema Fields)
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "Auditor",
    "description": "Read-only auditor role",
    "tenant_id": {{tenantId}},
    "is_active": true
}

### 3.4 List All Roles (with their assigned permissions)
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 3.5 Get Single Role Details & Permissions (by ID or Role Name)
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles/Branch%20Manager
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json


### ============================================================
### STEP 4. ADD / SYNC / REVOKE PERMISSIONS ON A ROLE
### ============================================================

### 4.1 List Available Menu Permissions (Label-Value format for frontend select)
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/access/permissions?module=Core&label_value=true
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### 4.2 Add Permissions to Role (mode: "add" - preserves existing permissions)
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles/assign-permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "Auditor",
    "mode": "add",
    "permissions": [
        "core.access.users.view",
        "core.access.roles.view",
        "core.tenancy.sites.view"
    ]
}

### 4.3 Revoke Specific Permissions from Role (mode: "revoke")
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles/assign-permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "Auditor",
    "mode": "revoke",
    "permissions": [
        "core.tenancy.sites.view"
    ]
}

### 4.4 Sync (Replace) All Permissions on Role (mode: "sync")
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/roles/assign-permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "role": "Auditor",
    "mode": "sync",
    "permissions": [
        "core.access.users.view",
        "core.access.permissions.view"
    ]
}


### ============================================================
### STEP 5. ASSIGN ROLE TO USER
### ============================================================

### 5.1 Register a New Test User
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/register
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "firstName": "Afnan",
    "lastName": "Khan",
    "email": "officer@primary.localhost",
    "password": "password123",
    "tenant_id": {{tenantId}},
    "site_id": {{siteId}},
    "role_id": "Support Officer"
}

### 5.2 Assign Role(s) to User(s) (Also clears user's cached menu automatically)
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/assign-roles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "user_ids": [{{userId}}],
    "roles": ["super-admin", "Branch Manager"],
    "replace_existing": false
}

### 5.3 Login as the New User to Verify Filtered Menu Based on Assigned Role
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/login
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "officer@primary.localhost",
    "password": "password123"
}


### ============================================================
### ADDITIONAL CRUD & AUTH ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================

### List Users
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Get User by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json

### Activate User
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": {{userId}}
}

### Deactivate User
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "id": {{userId}}
}

### Logout
POST {{baseUrl}}/core/access/users/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: application/json
